  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SYSTEMS AND METHODS TO DETECT ABNORMAL BEHAVIOR IN NETWORKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks is a set of technologies and techniques designed to identify and flag unusual patterns of activity within computer networks, crucial for preventing and detecting cyber-attacks and data breaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED STATES PATENT AND TRADEMARK OFFICE (USPTO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United States Patent and Trademark Office (USPTO) granted patent number 11277420 for 'Systems and methods to detect abnormal behavior in networks' on August 17, 2021."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;US11277420&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PATENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"US11277420 is a patent granted by the United States Patent and Trademark Office for 'Systems and methods to detect abnormal behavior in networks', describing a novel approach to detecting abnormal behavior in networks."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;S. GARCIA ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"S. Garcia et al. published a study in the Journal of Network and Computer Applications, which found that the use of anomaly detection systems can reduce the risk of cyber-attacks by up to 90%."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF NETWORK AND COMPUTER APPLICATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Journal of Network and Computer Applications published a study on anomaly detection systems, highlighting their effectiveness in reducing cyber-attack risks."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF STANDARDS AND TECHNOLOGY (NIST)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NIST recommends the use of anomaly detection systems as part of a comprehensive cybersecurity strategy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOMALY DETECTION IN COMPUTER NETWORKS: A SURVEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A survey on anomaly detection in computer networks, published in the Journal of Network and Computer Applications, discusses the effectiveness of such systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;USS _VIGILANT_&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"USS _Vigilant_ is a state-of-the-art naval vessel whose keel laying ceremony incorporated Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEWPORT NEWS SHIPBUILDING FACILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Newport News Shipbuilding facility is the location where the keel laying ceremony for the USS Vigilant took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Newport News Shipbuilding facility is the location where the keel laying ceremony for the USS _Vigilant_ took place on February 10, 2022."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. RACHEL KIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Rachel Kim is a co-inventor of the patented technology 'Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks' and emphasized the importance of securing shipboard networks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dr. Rachel Kim is a co-inventor of the patented technology and emphasized the importance of securing shipboard networks."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. JOHN LEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. John Lee is a co-inventor of the patented technology 'Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks' and contributed to its development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF NAVAL ENGINEERING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Journal of Naval Engineering published a study on enhancing shipboard security through advanced network monitoring, highlighting the significance of integrating advanced network security measures into modern shipbuilding."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARITIME NEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maritime News interviewed Dr. Rachel Kim, co-inventor of the patented technology, discussing the importance of securing shipboard networks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maritime News is a publication that conducted an interview with Dr. Rachel Kim regarding the importance of securing shipboard networks."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEBRUARY 10, 2022&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"February 10, 2022 is the date of the keel laying ceremony for the USS _Vigilant_."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUTTING-EDGE NAVAL VESSEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cutting-edge naval vessel is a state-of-the-art ship that incorporates advanced technologies, including Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEEL LAYING CEREMONY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Keel laying ceremony is a significant event in the construction of the USS Vigilant, taking place at Newport News Shipbuilding facility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The keel laying ceremony is a formal recognition of the start of a ship's construction, marking a significant milestone in the history of shipbuilding."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYBERSECURITY EXPERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cybersecurity experts Dr. Rachel Kim and Dr. John Lee developed the patented technology 'Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks'."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYBER-ATTACKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cyber-attacks are a type of malicious activity that can compromise the security and integrity of networked systems, which the technology aims to prevent and detect."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DATA BREACHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Data breaches are another form of malicious activity that the technology aims to prevent and detect, compromising the security and integrity of networked systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOMALOUS NETWORK BEHAVIOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anomalous network behavior refers to unusual patterns of activity within computer networks that the technology is designed to identify and flag."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REAL-TIME MONITORING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Real-time monitoring is a technique used by the technology to continuously analyze network traffic patterns and identify deviations from expected norms."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NETWORK TRAFFIC PATTERNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Network traffic patterns are the flow of data within a network that the technology analyzes to detect anomalies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEVIATIONS FROM EXPECTED NORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deviations from expected norms refer to unusual patterns of activity that the technology identifies as potential threats."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGNITARY APPEARANCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dignitary appearances are part of the keel laying ceremony, which is a formal recognition of the start of a ship's construction."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FESTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Festivities are part of the keel laying ceremony, which is a formal recognition of the start of a ship's construction."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYBERSECURITY TECHNOLOGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cybersecurity technologies include the Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks, which are crucial for preventing and detecting cyber-attacks and data breaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYBER THREATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cyber threats are the potential risks that the technology aims to mitigate, such as cyber-attacks and data breaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCED NETWORK SECURITY MEASURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced network security measures include the Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks, which are integrated into modern shipbuilding to enhance security."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATE-OF-THE-ART NAVAL VESSEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"State-of-the-art naval vessels are equipped with advanced technologies, including Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks, to ensure the integrity and security of their systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO-INVENTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Co-inventors are individuals who contribute to the development of a patented technology, such as Dr. Rachel Kim and Dr. John Lee for the Systems and Methods to Detect Abnormal Behavior in Networks."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An interview is a form of communication where Dr. Rachel Kim discussed the importance of securing shipboard networks with Maritime News."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;USS VIGILANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"USS Vigilant is a naval vessel that incorporated the patented technology into its systems, marking a significant step in vessel security."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATENTED TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patented Technology is the invention of Dr. Rachel Kim that was integrated into the USS Vigilant to enhance its security."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIST&quot;">
      <data key="d2">cb-0360</data>
      <data key="d1">"NIST recommends the use of anomaly detection systems, which aligns with the technology's application in enhancing cybersecurity strategies."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
